.TH AVR\-VM\-SSH 1 "" "avr 0.1.6" "Avrea CLI"
.SH NAME
avr-vm-ssh \- Open an SSH session to a RUNNING VM, or run a command on it.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B avr vm ssh
[OPTIONS] VM_ID [SSH_ARGS]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
Open an SSH session to a RUNNING VM, or run a command on it.
.PP
With no extra arguments this opens an interactive session. Anything after `--` is run as a remote command instead, e.g.:
.PP
avr vm ssh cvm-abc123 -- uname -a
.PP
The VM's host key is pinned from its endpoint, so the first connect neither prompts nor is spoofable. For port-forwarding use `avr vm port-forward`.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
\fIVM_ID\fR
\&
.TP
[\fISSH_ARGS...\fR]
\&
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-org\fR \fITEXT\fR
Organization ID. Uses default org if not specified (see: avr config set org).
.TP
\fB\-i\fR, \fB\-\-identity\fR \fIPATH\fR
Private key file to pass to ssh as -i.
.TP
\fB\-\-print\fR
Print the ssh command instead of running it.
